Essay on the relation between culture and lifestyle

Culture can be something someone believes, values, traditions,
language or customs. While a lifestyle is how a person lives 
their life, like what they eat for breakfast or dinner, what 
they wear to work or at home, how they behave or how they spend
their free time. Although these two things sound very different 
they still have many connections with each other.

Culture can teach individuals what to worship or who to love and
how to love them. Meaning lifestyle depends on culture, if your
catholic you might go to church every sunday or visit your family 
and help them around the house. So culture can change you lifestyle.

Some might argue that culture and lifestyle are not connected in any
shape or form. Saying that what if you don't believe in God or aren't 
religous. If so you could also have family traditions which contributes
to culture and changes your lifestyle.

In conclusion Culture and lifestyles are connected in atleast one way,
shape or form, even if you don't notice. All people do things different 
including you. 